# Mod Mallet report

Skyrim Special Edition 1.6.1170, script extender 2.2.6  
3 script extender plugins checked  
Mod manager: Vortex  
2 plugins and 1 archive read

> Your user name, your computer's name and the folders of your user account and your setup are replaced by placeholders such as %USERPROFILE% and <game>; mods, plugins and findings are unchanged.

## Placeholders

- `<game>`: the folder the game is installed in
- `<staging>`: the folder the mod manager keeps the installed mods in
- `<documents>`: the documents folder, where the game keeps saves and logs
- `%LOCALAPPDATA%`: the local application data of the user account
- `%APPDATA%`: the roaming application data of the user account

## Places read

- Game directory: `<game>` (from the entry the game's launcher wrote into the Windows registry)
- List of active plugins: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Skyrim Special Edition\plugins.txt` (at its standard place)
- Script extender log: `<documents>\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE\skse64.log` (at its standard place)
- Vortex's saved state: `%APPDATA%\Vortex\temp\state_backups_full\startup.json` (at its standard place)
- Vortex's folder of installed mods (the names of their files, and the files of the things you look at under Assets): `<staging>` (named in Vortex's list of deployed files)
- Folder of crash reports: `<documents>\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE` (not found)

## Errors and warnings

### Error (certain): Script extender plugin does not support this game version

Old.dll was switched off because it was not built for game version 1.6.1170.

- File: `data/skse/plugins/old.dll`
- Mod: Old Mod
- What to do: Look on the mod's page for a version built for your game version and install it. If there is none yet, disable the mod until it has been updated.
- Kind: `extender.plugin-incompatible`

